Author: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Description: Don't loop forever appending exactly the buffer capacity.
 ply_buffer_append_bytes() trimmed only appends longer than the capacity,
 so an append of exactly the capacity could never fit and the loop spun
 forever. terminal-write-queue.patch appends every terminal write.
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1145446
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-10

--- a/src/libply/ply-buffer.c
+++ b/src/libply/ply-buffer.c
@@ -187,7 +187,7 @@
         if (length == 0)
                 return;
 
-        if (length > PLY_BUFFER_MAX_BUFFER_CAPACITY) {
+        if (length >= PLY_BUFFER_MAX_BUFFER_CAPACITY) {
                 bytes += length - (PLY_BUFFER_MAX_BUFFER_CAPACITY - 1);
                 length = (PLY_BUFFER_MAX_BUFFER_CAPACITY - 1);
         }
